                  "content": "SELECTED: candidate_12\n\nCONFIDENCE: HIGH\n\nEXPLANATION:\nThe fix commit changes a single character range check in TextUtils.java:\n`(c >= 0xFE70 && c <= 0xFEFF)` -> `(c >= 0xFE70 && c <= 0xFEFE)`\nThis narrows the upper bound of one of the RTL unicode ranges by one code point so that\nU+FEFF (the special zero-width no-break space / BOM marker) is no longer classified as RTL.\n\nCandidate_12 is the commit that introduces the `isRTLCharacter(char c)` method (and the\nrelated `hasRTLCharacters`/`processBidi` helper methods) in TextUtils.java from scratch, as\npart of adding a new bidi/Arabic-reshaping text pipeline. The newly added method contains\nexactly the faulty range that the fix later corrects:\n\n    public static boolean isRTLCharacter(char c) {\n        //range of RTL characters per unicode specification\n        return (c >= 0x0590 && c <= 0x05FF) ||\n               (c >= 0xFB1D && c <= 0xFB4F) ||\n               (c >= 0x0600 && c <= 0x07BF) ||\n               (c >= 0xFB50 && c <= 0xFDFF) ||\n               (c >= 0xFE70 && c <= 0xFEFF)    ;\n    }\n\nNone of the earlier candidates (01, 02, 03, 04, 05, 06, 07, 08, 09, 10, 11) contain any\nreference to `isRTLCharacter` \u2014 the method and the surrounding bidi-handling code (including\nAndroidBidi.reorderAndReshapeBidiText, Styled.java's RTL reversal logic, and Canvas.java's\ndrawText routing through TextUtils.processBidi) do not exist prior to candidate_12. This\nconfirms candidate_12 is the first commit where the problematic `0xFE70`\u2013`0xFEFF` range check\nwas introduced, causing U+FEFF to be wrongly treated as an RTL character. Candidate_13\nhappens to contain a diff hunk identical to the fix commit's change (FEFF -> FEFE on the same\nline), which appears to be a duplicate/backport of the same fix already present in the\ncandidate history rather than a bug-introducing change \u2014 it modifies the line in the\ndirection of the correct fix, not toward the bug.\n"
                }
              }
